{
 "kind": "version",
 "id": "0.31",
 "title": "Empires at war",
 "date": "2026-11-11",
 "summary": "Version 0.31 turns the sector into a living galaxy of empires that trade, compete and go to war. Patch 0010 grew it to 58 systems and six empires with the Cycladic Isles, gave every empire its own stations and ships beside the neutral Independents, and replaced pledges with a reputation you earn. It added a commodities market and trade routes on the maps, war fleets that besiege stations until they burn or fall, gear with damage types, and landable planets and moons everywhere. It also redesigned the interface in amber, made every control rebindable with gamepad support, and turned the Library into an asset browser, all at 240 FPS or more. Patch 0011 gave wars teeth - combined invasions, distress calls and war missions - and added wrecks to salvage, fuel, the rings' local spaces, equipment screens by area, five new arms, save slots and autosaves, and a Talos reorganised around one rail that switches tools in a millisecond. Patch 0012 gave every empire its own story, look and people, made Kilon Alios the narrator of New Hellas with every line voiced, and added a loading screen and screens that fit at any text size. Then wounds, repairs and industry (patch 0013). Patch 0014 made everything stream: the game in a browser and on phones, no loading screens, procedural placeholders, chunked planets, streamed systems with surfaces built ahead, a memory pool with its console, and a liquid health gauge. Patch 0015 brought navigation reports to sell across the galaxy, placeholders on planets, a fuel ring on the gauge, one tabbed console and probes moved as a group. Then patch 0016 turned the game 3D: planets of real ground to land on and walk, stations docked by hand, towns, caves and dungeons, photoreal characters. Then mining, digging and the Minoan look (patch 0017). Then living stations and the law (patch 0018). Then a sandbox galaxy (patch 0019). Then build your own (patch 0020). Then the web build starts (patch 0021). Then loading in the browser (patch 0022).",
